# Flutter & bloc

## Structure

Feature-first under `lib/`:

- `data/models/`, `data/repositories/`
- `features/<feature>/` (pages + Cubit/Bloc)
- `widgets/` for shared UI

Keep game rules in models (`Level`), not in widgets.

## State

- Cubit for simple load/list; Bloc + sealed events for gameplay.
- Events and states extend `Equatable`; use immutable `copyWith` / deep clones for boards.

```dart
// ✅ GOOD — sealed event, Equatable props
sealed class GameEvent extends Equatable {
  const GameEvent();
  @override
  List<Object?> get props => [];
}
```

## Board coordinates

Indices are `[x][y]` (column, row), matching the Android original. Never flip axes when porting or editing levels.

Tap → toggle `selected` → `Level.recalcFills()` (XOR 3×3 brush). Done when board fills match `tableModel`.

## Tests & lints

- Stamp/XOR or level JSON changes → update `test/level_logic_test.dart`.
- Follow `flutter_lints`; prefer small, colocated feature files.
